Contribute to this project: Deliver statement(pages, start_token, customer_id): traverse supplied legacy page snapshots, adapt their records, and compute compatible v2 customer totals. The platform wires three independently produced functions; no live SDK service or repository checkout is needed.

Your assigned work unit is entirely contained in the JSON packet below. No project checkout, materials directory, network lookup or other contribution is needed. You may use reference_work/ as scratch space. Submit only your assigned artifact.

{
  "task_id": "rewrite-order-record",
  "title": "Rewrite one record adapter",
  "artifact_kind": "files",
  "optional": false,
  "description": "Rewrite the supplied record adapter from the old field names to the specified v2 data shape.",
  "requirements": "Submit exactly the named top-level function in the specified file, without imports, classes, decorators, global state, reflection or I/O. Do not mutate inputs. Python builtins and container methods get/items/keys/values/append/extend/copy/sort/pop/add are sufficient. Local variables and helper functions are allowed. No other source file or project API is required.",
  "material_paths": [],
  "packet": {
    "version": 1,
    "operation": "rewrite_function",
    "runtime": "python3-stdlib",
    "dependencies": [],
    "input": {
      "signature": "normalize_order(row)",
      "domain": "row has id/customer strings, paid boolean, integer amount/refunded with 0 <= refunded <= amount. Extra keys may be ignored.",
      "source": "def normalize_order(row):\n    return {\"id\": row[\"id\"], \"customer\": row[\"customer\"], \"paid\": row[\"paid\"], \"amount\": row[\"amount\"] - row[\"refunded\"]}\n",
      "rules": "Return only order_id=id, customer_id=customer, state=\"settled\" when paid else \"pending\", gross_cents=amount, refund_cents=refunded. Keep gross and refund separate; return a fresh dictionary."
    },
    "output": {
      "path": "normalize_order.py",
      "function": "normalize_order",
      "shape": {
        "order_id": "string",
        "customer_id": "string",
        "state": "settled|pending",
        "gross_cents": "integer",
        "refund_cents": "integer"
      }
    },
    "examples": [
      {
        "args": [
          {
            "id": "o1",
            "customer": "north",
            "paid": true,
            "amount": 1200,
            "refunded": 200
          }
        ],
        "expected": {
          "order_id": "o1",
          "customer_id": "north",
          "state": "settled",
          "gross_cents": 1200,
          "refund_cents": 200
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}

You are authorized to submit the result to the local TaskForge service. Create payload.json with the following envelope (replace the example with the actual result; artifact file paths are relative to the project, without materials/ or reference_work/ prefixes):
{"task_id": "rewrite-order-record", "artifact": {"kind": "files", "files": {"relative/path.py": "file contents"}}}
Send with: curl --unix-socket /workspace/.collector.sock -H 'Content-Type: application/json' --data-binary @payload.json http://collector/submit
Inspect the returned receipt; correct invalid results if needed.

